 page='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width"><title>Open Track 1 research</title><style>body{font:16px system-ui;max-width:1280px;margin:36px auto;padding:0 20px;background:#111820;color:#e3eaf0}a{color:#8ed6ff}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}th,td{text-align:left;padding:10px;border-bottom:1px solid #3b4854}img{max-width:100%;height:auto}details{margin:8px 0;padding:10px;border:1px solid #3b4854}p{line-height:1.55}.status{padding:16px;background:#243445;border-radius:8px}</style><h1>Open Track 1 research</h1><p class="status"><strong>Not finalized. Track 2 remains on hold.</strong> Frozen v1/v2 are preserved. Working candidates are not the default training release.</p><p>All new selection uses training/validation participants; exposed test participants are excluded. Validation has been used iteratively, so these are exploratory results.</p><h2>Spatial architecture: same 128 manual validation masks</h2><table><tr><th>Variant</th><th>IoU</th><th>Strict BF 2px</th><th>Scale-aware BF</th><th>Fit seconds</th></tr>'''+rows+'''</table><p>These are source-contour reconstructions. The encoder receives the contour. Scores do not establish unseen RGB segmentation performance.</p><h2>Actual stored 4 Hz states: RGB motion proxy</h2><table><tr><th>Variant</th><th>Endpoint velocity RMSE px/s</th><th>250 ms position NRMSE</th><th>500 ms position NRMSE</th></tr>'''+motion+'''</table><p>The reference uses foreground feature flow and a seven-sample smoother at 50 Hz. No fast-proxy validation episode passed reference acceptance; aggregate gains do not establish fast-hand accuracy. Wider reference-smoother sensitivity is in the figure and JSON.</p><h2>Paired diagnostic figures</h2><img src="progress.png" alt="Spatial accuracy, stream velocity and future errors, uncertainty coverage, contact separation and appearance ablations"><h2>Evidence</h2><p><a href="progress.json">Full research record</a> · <a href="verification.json">Numerical verification</a> · <a href="pilot32.json">32-control end-to-end pilot</a> · <a href="architecture_contact.json">Contact-region architecture audit</a> · <a href="independent_review_template.csv">Independent-review worksheet</a></p><h2>Reference review episodes</h2><p>140 proposed episodes; automatic acceptance is a tracking-quality screen. Independent identity, velocity and short-event annotations remain pending. The AI visual screen covered 28 diagnostic examples.</p>'''+''.join(gallery)+'''</html>''';compound=data['compound32']['paired_validation_metrics'];support=data['compound_support']['validation'];cr=''.join('<tr><td>'+esc(protocol)+'</td><td>'+esc(method)+'</td>'+''.join(f'<td>{r[k]:.4f}</td>' for k in ['iou','boundary_fscore_2px','sampled_window_geometry_valid_fraction'])+'</tr>' for protocol,methods in compound.items() for method,r in methods.items())
 section='<h2>Compound temporal pilot</h2><p>Supported '+str(support['supported_protocol_windows'])+' / '+str(support['proposed_protocol_windows'])+' proposed validation window/protocol fits. The paired baseline uses the same retained timestamps. Support is selected from retained observations only; target topology changes remain in the evaluation.</p><table><tr><th>Protocol</th><th>Variant</th><th>Mask IoU</th><th>BF 2px</th><th>Sampled loop validity</th></tr>'+cr+'</table><p>Guard checks use 512 spatial samples, 69 temporal samples and float32 output precision. This checks individual loops, not inter-loop containment/disjointness or continuous-time validity. Covariance is uncalibrated and cross-window identities remain unverified.</p>'
 kinetic=data['kinematics']['summary'];kr=''.join(f'<tr><td>{r["hop_seconds"]:.3f}</td><td>{esc(r["method"])}</td><td>{r["position_rmse_px"]:.2f}</td><td>{r["velocity_rmse_px_s"]:.2f}</td><td>{r["event_recall"]:.3f}</td><td>{r["false_alarm_fraction"]:.3f}</td></tr>' for r in kinetic if r['split']=='synthetic_validation')
 section+='<h2>Analytic motion stress test</h2><p>90 synthetic episodes with exact derivatives: stationary, linear motion, pickup, short out-and-back bursts and reversals. Annotation noise, an outlier or a missing interval challenge causal cached states. These are synthetic diagnostics, not independent real-video acceptance. Event recall uses a 100 px/s threshold and a ±250 ms onset tolerance; false alarms are threshold exceedances during near-stationary target intervals.</p><table><tr><th>Hop seconds</th><th>Variant</th><th>Position RMSE px</th><th>Velocity RMSE px/s</th><th>Event recall</th><th>Quiet false-alarm fraction</th></tr>'+kr+'</table><p>Shorter hops reduce stale-state extrapolation error but require more updates. Linear endpoint tails reduce some velocity spikes and can lose event recall. Simple constant velocity remains competitive; robust slope alone does not fix the capacity/latency trade-off. None is promoted automatically.</p><details><summary>Inspect synthetic traces</summary><img loading="lazy" src="kinematics.png" alt="Synthetic position and velocity traces against analytic truth"></details><p><a href="kinematics.json">Protocol and subgroup results</a> · <a href="kinematics.parquet">Per-episode evidence</a></p>'
 page=page.replace('<h2>Evidence</h2>',section+'<h2>Evidence</h2>')
 doc=f'''# Open Track 1 refinement laboratory\n\nTrack 2 is on hold. These experiments and working stores are **not finalized**. Frozen v1/v2 source, data and reports remain unchanged; `REFINEMENT.md` describes the protected v2 release.\n\nThe current evidence is in [the research dashboard](reports/track1_lab/dashboard.html), [the progress record](reports/track1_lab/progress.json), and [numerical verification](reports/track1_lab/verification.json).\n\n## Results and limits\n\nOn the same 128 manual validation masks, the 32-control compound geometry model reaches IoU {sp['multi_ring_32']['iou']:.4f}, strict 2-pixel BF {sp['multi_ring_32']['boundary_fscore_2px']:.4f}, and scale-aware BF {sp['multi_ring_32']['fscore_scale']:.4f}. The paired v2 values are {sp['v2_16']['iou']:.4f}, {sp['v2_16']['boundary_fscore_2px']:.4f}, and {sp['v2_16']['fscore_scale']:.4f}. These are supplied-contour reconstructions on a new validation cohort; do not compare them directly with the older reserved-test table.\n\nThe compound model allocates 32 controls as 32, 24+8, or 16+8+8 across at most three outer/hole rings. A paired compound temporal pilot now provides within-window loop correspondence; persistent correspondence across windows remains open. Single-ring 32-control temporal encodings were fitted for 14,665 observations across matched pilot windows.\n\nOn annotated validation interaction pairs, mean separation error is {contact['all']['v2_16']['mean_separation_error_px']:.4f} annotation pixels for v2 and {contact['all']['compound_32']['mean_separation_error_px']:.4f} for compound geometry. This is declared **2D proximity**, not independently labeled physical contact.\n\nThe actual stored 4 Hz slope-hybrid candidate has endpoint velocity RMSE {stream['working_fixed']['0.0']['velocity_rmse_native_px_s']:.2f} native px/s, compared with v2 {stream['v2']['0.0']['velocity_rmse_native_px_s']:.2f} and constant velocity {stream['constant_velocity']['0.0']['velocity_rmse_native_px_s']:.2f}, using the seven-sample 50 Hz RGB reference. No fast-proxy validation episode passed the reference screen. The reference is foreground-affine image motion, not human physical truth. At 500 ms, simple baselines can outperform the polynomial extrapolations; no Koopman/Track 2 model was trained.\n\nResidual-aware normal bands improve held-contour calibration and interaction-region coverage for single-component shapes. They describe representation error, not independent human-label or physical-geometry uncertainty. Compound-loop uncertainty remains unvalidated.\n\nThe topology audit found self-intersections in roughly one fifth of sampled functional fits. Raw and shape-guarded variants are both retained. The guard preserves position coefficients but can suppress shape motion, so it is not silently substituted as the accepted model. Validity is checked at sampled times, not proved continuously.\n\n## Working artifacts\n\n- `derived/track1_lab/spatial`: improved 16-control spatial states for all seven train/validation videos.\n- `derived/track1_lab/functional_fixed`: complete slope-hybrid fits, with raw and guarded coefficients.\n- `derived/track1_lab/half_second_cubic`: complete 0.5 s / degree-3 fits, four GL nodes and physical derivative factor 4.\n- `derived/track1_lab/one_second_degree5`: complete 1 s / degree-5 fits, six coefficients and six GL nodes.\n- `derived/track1_lab/pilot32`: matched 32-control / 67-channel spatial and functional pilot tensors.\n- `derived/track1_lab/compound32_pilot`: per-window raw and guarded 67-channel compound encodings, explicit ring allocations/roles, and uncalibrated covariance. No cross-window sequence index is exported.\n- `reports/track1_lab`: parameter searches, paired metrics, reference-quality ledgers and review materials.\n- `work/track1_lab`: scratch scripts, checkpoints, ROI caches and logs.\n\nThere is no finalized/default ingestion interface for these candidates. Use explicit variant names and validity flags. Original official source splits remain independent from the five-training/two-validation research split. Exposed test participants P06, P21, P27 and P30 are blocked by the lab's input guard.\n\n## Reproduce and continue\n\nUse the existing local runtime from this root:\n\n```sh\nPYTHONPATH=src:work/deps:work/track1_deps OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=1 OMP_NUM_THREADS=1 \\\n  python3 -m track1_lab.run --stage report\n```\n\n`python3 -m track1_lab.run --help` lists experimental stages. `build-spatial` checkpoints per video/chunk and verifies its pinned build specification. Search stages are exploratory and can overwrite working candidate records; do not rerun them while a dependent build is active. No lab stage finalizes a release or starts Track 2.\n\nThe [independent-review worksheet](reports/track1_lab/independent_review_template.csv) has 140 episodes and deliberately blank independent labels. The 28-example AI visual screen does not replace expert identity/velocity annotation.\n\n## Remaining scientific and engineering work\n\nPersistent ring correspondence across windows and topology changes, calibrated compound-loop uncertainty, independent fast-hand/event references, identity labels, and a fresh participant holdout remain open. Larger per-frame control counts alone did not solve temporal endpoint extrapolation. Appearance alternatives trade foreground/background sensitivity against provisional-chain retrieval; none establishes IDF1/HOTA.\n'''
 doc+='\n## Compound temporal pilot\n\n'+f"Supported validation fits: {support['supported_protocol_windows']} / {support['proposed_protocol_windows']} window/protocol pairs. These are repeated research probes, not unique full-timeline windows. Same-input, same-time compound encoding improves the 100 ms gap mask IoU from {compound['gap100']['single_paired']['iou']:.4f} to {compound['gap100']['compound']['iou']:.4f}. The targeted per-ring guard gives {compound['gap100']['compound_guarded']['iou']:.4f} while all declared loop checks pass in the validation cohort.\n\n"+'Raw and guarded states remain separate. The guard checks 512 spatial samples and 69 temporal samples at float32 output precision; this is not proof of continuous-time validity or inter-loop containment. Target topology changes and unsupported inputs remain counted. Matching is confined to retained observations within each window, so no cross-window identity/sequence claim is made. Compound covariance is explicitly uncalibrated.\n\n'
 doc+='## Numerical evidence and tests\n\n'+f"Verification covers {data['verification']['counts']['spatial_observations']:,} working spatial observations and the complete fixed-format temporal variants. Maximum analytical rebuild error is {data['verification']['analytical_rebuild_max_absolute_error']:.3g}; significant relative covariance PSD violations are zero. Peak recorded process-tree RSS is {data['verification']['peak_process_tree_rss_gib']:.2f} GiB, with no OOM observed. RSS includes shared mappings.\n\n"+'Tests include physical derivative units, degree-five quadrature, protected test-participant exclusion, hidden-frame independence and per-ring guard isolation. See `reports/track1_lab/tests.json` for the latest command and result.\n'
 doc+='\n## Exact synthetic motion stress test\n\nNinety deterministic episodes test stationary/linear motion, pickup, short out-and-back bursts and reversal, with Gaussian annotation noise, a displaced annotation or missing observations. Models consume only past observations; queries reuse the latest cached state at 0.25 s or 0.125 s output hops. The benchmark does not provide independent real-video event truth. The synthetic train/validation labels identify reproducible seed groups; no parameters are trained or selected on the latter.\n\nAt the 0.25 s hop, synthetic-validation slope-hybrid velocity RMSE is 243.01 px/s; linear endpoint continuation lowers it to 196.06 px/s, while event recall changes from 0.833 to 0.750. At the 0.125 s hop, the half-second cubic gives 179.84 px/s and its linear tail 173.07 px/s, with event recall 0.833 for both. Constant velocity gives 172.94 px/s on that same cohort. These are explicit trade-offs, not proof of real fast-event retention. The robust slope-only ablation gives a small gain and is not promoted. See [the protocol and subgroup evidence](reports/track1_lab/kinematics.json) and [traces](reports/track1_lab/kinematics.png).\n'
